{"severity":"warning","file":"errors/copy_shared_5.march","start_line":9,"start_col":22,"end_line":9,"end_col":24,"message":"`List.map` builds a new copy instead of reusing `xs` in place, because a closure captured `xs`.\nA closure keeps its own reference to every value it captures, since it may run more than once, so a call inside it never holds the only reference to `xs`.","code":"copy_shared","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/copy_shared_5.march","start_line":9,"start_col":4,"end_line":9,"end_col":40,"message":"this closure captures `xs`"}],"notes":[],"category":"COPY"}
